    writing_through_both_guards_while_both_are_live          GREEN  (misses it)
    four_tile_columns_the_way_the_decoder_holds_them         GREEN  (misses it)
    a_row_reference_survives_the_next_column_taking_one      UB     (catches it)
    an_immutable_rectangle_does_not_alias_a_neighbours_write UB     (catches it)
    control_per_row_guards_from_two_tile_columns             GREEN  (correct)
    control_one_hull_guard_is_exclusive                      GREEN  (correct)
    the_rows_handed_out_are_exactly_the_rectangle            GREEN  (correct)

The two cases that CAUGHT the original defect do not catch the transient form,
because each of their row references dies at the end of its own statement.
That is why the two "held across the next retag" cases exist; do not delete
them as duplicates.

