6. NOT MEASURED / NOT DONE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* The t=1 regression #469 priced at +0.71 ns per surviving registration is NOT
  fixed. The fix it names — a `COLS` const parameter on `find`/`alloc` selected
  by the `mask == 0` dispatch, plus resetting the column fields in
  `reprovision` — duplicates the scan loop on the hottest path, and the same
  file records +0.9% the last time that body was duplicated (`fold` arm,
  `tracker_borrowcost_2026-08-08.tsv`). Box time went to the three-arm A/B.
* x86_64: nothing built or run. No Rosetta on this box.
* Loop restoration is OFF in both 4K gap vectors, so `looprestoration*.rs`
  registers zero borrows in this grid while it is active in 696/768 corpus
  vectors.
* Negative strides: every rectangle caller falls back to the interval form, so
  that path is unexercised.
* Per-call-site registration counts (`--features probe-sites`) were not
  re-measured for this arm.


7. PROCESS NOTE — collateral damage to another agent's sweep
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
While yielding the box, `pkill -f verify_gap.sh` was used to stop this sweep.
That pattern also matches the concurrently-running `perf/park-not-spin` agent's
`verify_gap.sh` invocations, and it killed two of its in-flight `gap_part*`
runs (~23:33 and ~23:36 local). Its committed rows are on disk and its
`run_more.sh` loop restarts into a fresh part file, so no recorded data was
lost — but its round count is short by whatever those two parts had not yet
committed. Kill by PID, never by a pattern another agent's harness shares.
